      "content": "Mahatma Gandhi (1869–1948)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Mahatma Gandhi (1869–1948) was a central figure in the Indian independence movement.",
        "Subhas Chandra Bose (1897–1945) led prominent nationalist efforts for Indian independence.",
        "Bhagat Singh (1907–1931) stands as one of the most prominent revolutionary figures.",
        "The 'Lal-Bal-Pal' triumvirate consisted of Lala Lajpat Rai (1865–1928), Bal Gangadhar Tilak (1856–1920), and Bipin Chandra Pal (1858–1932).",
        "Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel (1875–1950) and Jawaharlal Nehru (1889–1964) played critical roles in shaping modern India."
      ],
      "id": "6h1lw5o"
